"patch_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy2-stubs/pull/59.patch","merged_at":"2021-04-12T18:33:05Z"},"body":"<!-- Provide a general summary of your proposed changes in the Title field above -->\r\n\r\n### Description\r\nI've expanded the type hints for the ordering list while testing for https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6205.\r\n\r\n### Checklist\r\nThis pull request is:\r\n\r\n- [ ] A documentation / typographical error fix\r\n\t- Good to go, no issue or tests are needed\r\n- [x] A short code fix\r\n\t- please include the issue number, and create an issue if none exists, which\r\n\t  must include a complete example of the issue.  one line code fixes without an\r\n\t  issue and demonstration will not be accepted.\r\n\t- Please include: `Fixes: #<issue number>` in the commit message\r\n\t- please include tests.   one line code fixes without tests will not be accepted.\r\n- [ ] A new feature implementation\r\n\t- please include the issue number, and create an issue if none exists, which must\r\n\t  include a complete example of how the feature would look.\r\n\t- Please include: `Fixes: #<issue number>` in the commit message\r\n\t- please include tests.\r\n\r\n**Have a nice day!**\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy2-stubs/issues/59/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy2-stubs/issues/59/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/815865782","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6205#issuecomment-815865782","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/6205","id":815865782,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgxNTg2NTc4Mg==","user":{"login":"MaicoTimmerman","id":904824,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNDgyNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/904824?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman","html_url":"https://github.com/MaicoTimmerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-04-08T14:22:00Z","updated_at":"2021-04-08T14:24:21Z","body":"@zzzeek It seems that my initial report here is incorrect/incomplete. The `relationship.collection_class` should be a class or callable, not an instance of that class. I mixed that up while creating a minimal reproduction sample. \r\n\r\nHowever, it seems that mypy  does not pick up the annotation that it should be a [`Type`](https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy2-stubs/blob/b0afe353927feed67df8aaefa9cdc4339503fcf6/sqlalchemy-stubs/orm/relationships.pyi#L63). I'm not sure if that is an error in de stubs or that the plugin's functionality for the `relationship` ignores the stub typing.\r\n\r\nThe fix for this issue is that it should either take a type (which is functioning correctly in the 1.4.6 release) or a callable. See https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy2-stubs/pull/59 for reference:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nparent = relationship(\"A\", collection_class=lambda: OrderingList(\"ordering\")) # not exposed in __all__\r\nparent = relationship(\"A\", collection_class=ordering_list(\"position\")) # equivalent, exposed in __all__\r\n```\r\n\r\nNot related to the mypy plugin, but using `sqlalchemy.ext.OrderingList(\"ordering\")` directly results in errors as the `ordering_attr` is not actually set. Shall I open a new issue for that? Note that this has also made it into the new test case in 64cfcf4af0d5b09efa07aeb2b863c2aae9587c3d","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/815865782/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"MaicoTimmerman","id":904824,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNDgyNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/904824?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman","html_url":"https://github.com/MaicoTimmerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaicoTimmerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":4569012327,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50NDU2OTAxMjMyNw==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/4569012327","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek